-- chem/frustration.cub — the local certificate of a fold is of its native energy, and designable sequences are
-- frustration free. In the HP model of chem/selection.cub the energy is minus the number of H–H contacts, a sum of
-- local terms, one per pair of residues the lattice lets touch ((0,3), (0,5), (1,4), (2,5) at six residues). Each term
-- is at least −1 when both residues are H and 0 otherwise, so E_s(c) ≥ −u(s) for every fold, u(s) the number of such
-- H–H pairs: a local lower certificate, exact (zero defect) when some fold makes every such pair touch at once, which
-- is the fold being frustration free (Bryngelson and Wolynes's minimal frustration at its extreme). Computed over
-- all 64 sequences (`fr-table`): each of the 7 designable sequences (a unique native fold with a contact) has
-- m(s) = u(s), its native satisfying every local term; of the 33 other sequences with u ≥ 1, 23 also reach m = u
-- (frustration free, but with more than one fold at the minimum) and 10 are frustrated (m < u). So designable implies
-- frustration free here, not conversely: uniqueness of the minimum is the further condition (the gap δE).
import "freedual.cub"

